ization really  means um it's actually the technological  equivalent of democracy  so it is actually a very interesting  concept because it kind of gives the  authority of regulating a system back to  the individual user  so  so i think when we do it when we do  something you know that involves the  users of a system a lot of things can be  done such as like contracts between  users  you know getting the users involved in  dispute resolution processes so there  are a lot of opportunities when you give  the power back to the user and get the  user themselves to p to be part of an  innovative solution so that's where yeah  no i was going to say along those lines  what's in the sponsi ecosystem that  allows that to happen  right right yeah so um yeah so i think  um we are utilizing blockchain in a  couple of very  niche areas but um they actually solved  the traditional workflow processes we  had problems with in the past so the  first thing is of course digital  resolution so um just imagine this um an  influencer and a business has a dispute  about like payment about deliverables  this this is quite common in the  industry right yeah so  yeah so you know who is to decide um who  is the one who's right here and who is  the one who's wrong especially when  money is involved you know both parties  might not accept you know a third party  solution  but what if what if the general public  or what if the users of the ecosystem  get a say in the decision that's being  made for this dispute itself  so um i think it's a very fair you know  mechanism itself um so yeah and in  spawnc we have something called the jury  protocol so um the jury protocol is  basically just like you know how you  have in the course in the us you have  like a jury based system right so the  members of the public can vote on the  outcome of a system and that is what  sponsee is trying to do and not just  that but we're also leveraging you know  like machine learning models to get the  public to train 